      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Variation in insulin and C peptide levels was examined in patients with angina of new onset and chronic coronary heart disease. Insulin secretion was increased in all coronary patients, as compared to the controls, and hormonal response to additional stress was abnormal in postmyocardial infarction patients. It is demonstrated that insulin secretion is already changed at early stages of coronary disease, and the pattern of change is presented."},
